  "body": "Found while working #31 (PR #1314) on macOS.\n\nWhat happens: `web/build-app-wasm.sh` stops on a stock Mac for two reasons.\n- It calls `sed -i` in GNU form (no suffix argument). BSD sed reads the next argument as the backup suffix and fails or edits the wrong thing.\n- Line ~104 expands `\"${PROFILE_ARGS[@]}\"` while the array is empty under `set -u`. bash 3.2, the macOS `/bin/bash`, treats that as an unbound variable and exits.\n\nExpected: the script runs on Linux, macOS (bash 3.2, BSD sed) and Git Bash alike.\n\nFix: use `sed -i.bak ... && rm -f *.bak` (or a temp file plus `mv`), and expand the array as `${PROFILE_ARGS[@]+\"${PROFILE_ARGS[@]}\"}`.\n\nDone means: `web/build-app-wasm.sh` and `web/check-app-page.sh` run unmodified on macOS with /bin/bash and BSD sed.\n",
